WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.690
This is Chief Joseph,

2
00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:06.990
a leader and the best-known spokesman
of the Nez Perce during the war of 1877,

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.660
when about eight hundred Nez Perce
men, women, and children

4
00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.180
tried to escape the U.S. Army
in a fighting retreat

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.850
of nearly twelve hundred miles toward Canada.

6
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.310
The military leadership was shared
among several chiefs.

7
00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.690
Joseph was above all a guardian
of his people, and a diplomat.

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.430
After his surrender,

9
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.330
he spent the rest of his life campaigning
for his people's right to go home.

10
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:35.390
Curtis photographed him in 1903, in regalia,
with none of that struggle in view.
